	)
	(text "Every multimeter output is read through 100k (series) into a 74HCT165 input, with a\n100k pull-down on the connector side:\n - TTL-compatible thresholds for the 7404 outputs of the 70754 unit\n - < 35 uA per line into the input clamp diodes when the isolated supply is off\n   (USB unplugged), so the multimeter cannot back-power this board\n - defined (all-zero) data when the board is not plugged into the multimeter\n\nWhich input reads which SKB pin was chosen for the shortest board layout\n(scripts/optimise.py); the firmware uses the table below.\n\nSerial stream at MISO after a LATCH pulse; bit 0 is shifted out first.\nNumbers are SKB pins, \"=1\" / \"=0\" are hard-wired marker bits (chain length check).\n  bit  0.. 7  U10 D7..D0 :   2  18  35  36  34   1   3  19\n  bit  8..15  U11 D7..D0 :  22  38   5  20  21   4   6  23\n  bit 16..23  U12 D7..D0 :  26  27  24  25   7   8   9  10\n  bit 24..31  U13 D7..D0 :  14  31  29  28  12  11  13  30\n  bit 32..39  U14 D7..D0 :  =1  =0  =0  33  16  32  17  15\nSKB 38 is the read-back of the FRONT PANEL LOCKOUT line (high = DVM powered)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 240 190 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4cabf1f3-1cba-5547-99e5-829a7f5ad8b7")
	)
	(text "100k pull-downs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 232.94 33.5 0)
